// Practice quiz: Serving pipeline results as an API
// Formative, low-stakes retention practice. First draft, not reviewed. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: python/fastapi-services/serving-pipeline-results-as-an-api

::o1 hide field::A query returns an internal email column, but clients must not see it. What is the most direct control in the route? {
~Ask clients to ignore the field #Not quite. The data would still leave your service.
~Rename the column to private_email #Not quite. A new name does not stop it being sent.
~Use POST instead of GET #Not quite. The method does not limit fields.
=Declare a response_model without that field #Correct. The returned data is filtered through the model on the way out.
}

::o1 read only::Which set of routes fits a read-only results service? {
=GET routes only #Correct. GET retrieves data; the pipeline owns the writes.
~GET and DELETE routes #Not quite. DELETE changes data.
~POST routes that update rows #Not quite. Those change data.
~PUT routes for every table #Not quite. PUT changes data.
}

::o2 missing::A record is not found. What should the route do? {
~return None #Not quite. With a response model, returning None does not tell the client it is missing, and it may fail validation.
=raise HTTPException(status_code\=404, detail\="...") #Correct. The client gets a clear status and message.
~return \{"error"\: "missing"\} with status 200 #Not quite. A 200 tells clients the request succeeded.
~print a message and return an empty dict #Not quite. The client cannot tell what happened.
}

::o2 limit bound::Why declare limit with Query(20, ge\=1, le\=100)? {
~It caches 100 rows #Not quite. It only validates the parameter.
~It makes limit a path parameter #Not quite. Query declares a query parameter.
=It rejects a request asking for too many rows, or for none #Correct. Out-of-range values get a 422 before your query runs.
~It sorts the results #Not quite. Sorting belongs in your SQL.
}

::o3 override::What does app.dependency_overrides[get_db] \= fake do? {
~Deletes get_db from your module #Not quite. The function is untouched; only the app's lookup changes.
~Runs get_db and then fake #Not quite. Only the override runs.
=Makes FastAPI call fake instead of get_db for routes that depend on it #Correct. This swaps the dependency without changing the routes.
~Applies only to production traffic #Not quite. It applies to the app object, usually in tests, until cleared.
}
